1
00:00:14,681 --> 00:00:17,142
Something's off. I don't like this.

2
00:00:18,143 --> 00:00:20,687
The enemy has activated a Stand.

3
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:24,190
I can feel its presence.

4
00:00:24,274 --> 00:00:27,944
But our enemy isn't in this city.

5
00:00:28,027 --> 00:00:30,613
I can feel it moving farther away.

6
00:00:30,697 --> 00:00:32,907
If it wanted to attack us,

7
00:00:32,991 --> 00:00:34,743
its presence should be
approaching us instead.

8
00:00:35,910 --> 00:00:37,078
What is going on?

9
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:48,590
There's my body!

10
00:00:49,257 --> 00:00:54,262
The enemy first wants to kill my body,
which is vulnerable without my Stand.

11
00:00:54,345 --> 00:00:56,848
I have to protect my body!

12
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,019
What's this?

13
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:38,575
Oh! It's Batman!

14
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:40,702
I found Batman! Awesome!

15
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:42,328
EPISODE 26: BOHEMIAN ECSTATIC (2)

16
00:02:43,496 --> 00:02:47,542
Shit, why won't my body stay still?

17
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:52,755
Weather, do you not see me

18
00:02:52,839 --> 00:02:55,758
because you aren't under
the enemy Stand's influence?

19
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:58,511
Weather, I'm going after my body.

20
00:02:59,053 --> 00:03:01,014
You go hunt down the Stand User!

21
00:03:02,432 --> 00:03:03,349
Anastasia,

22
00:03:04,142 --> 00:03:05,184
where are you?

23
00:03:08,855 --> 00:03:10,440
Scoundrel!

24
00:03:10,523 --> 00:03:13,359
How could you show your face
after what you've done?

25
00:03:13,443 --> 00:03:15,111
I'll call the police right now!

26
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:18,531
Hello, is this the police?

27
00:03:18,615 --> 00:03:22,118
Wait just a moment.
Were you talking about me?

28
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:24,746
Stay the hell away from my shop!

29
00:03:24,829 --> 00:03:27,332
Calm down. How about this?

30
00:03:27,415 --> 00:03:30,585
I'm short on time
and I need to speak to you.

31
00:03:30,668 --> 00:03:34,631
The hell that's enough!
You smashed up my tables!

32
00:03:34,714 --> 00:03:37,342
I've got no wife.
I run this place all by myself!

33
00:03:37,425 --> 00:03:40,094
What? So my body came here?

34
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:41,387
If it's money you want,

35
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:43,640
just tell me the amount, and I'll pay.

36
00:03:43,723 --> 00:03:45,850
So please, hang up the phone.

37
00:03:46,559 --> 00:03:48,061
Tell me, where did I go?

38
00:03:48,144 --> 00:03:49,229
I need to know.

39
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:56,778
I mean, that was my twin younger brother.

40
00:03:56,861 --> 00:04:00,073
Is something the matter?
Is there a problem here?

41
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:02,408
This is Squad 6.

42
00:04:02,492 --> 00:04:06,496
We're following up on a tip
about an escaped convict.

43
00:04:06,579 --> 00:04:07,413
Roger that.

44
00:04:08,122 --> 00:04:10,792
Excuse me, can you turn around?

45
00:04:13,378 --> 00:04:15,129
That's me!

46
00:04:15,213 --> 00:04:17,882
My body is still inside the shop!

47
00:04:17,966 --> 00:04:19,425
Turn around.

48
00:04:19,509 --> 00:04:22,345
Show your face and answer my questions.

49
00:04:24,347 --> 00:04:26,099
It's business as usual,

50
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:28,601
Officer.

51
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:34,357
Sorry, you may go.

52
00:04:37,443 --> 00:04:39,320
Wasn't there an old man here?

53
00:04:39,946 --> 00:04:43,992
Diver Drive!
I injected chocolate into my face.

54
00:04:44,826 --> 00:04:49,372
Breaking news.
The famous Japanese character Kenshiro

55
00:04:49,455 --> 00:04:54,460
defeated Raoh the villain
after a showdown in West Shinjuku, Tokyo!

56
00:04:54,544 --> 00:04:58,006
The sequence of events followed
the original works…

57
00:04:58,089 --> 00:05:00,633
Where are you? Show yourself!

58
00:05:00,717 --> 00:05:03,052
- Hurray!
- Princess is awake!

59
00:05:03,678 --> 00:05:06,097
Snow White returned to us!

60
00:05:06,180 --> 00:05:08,016
The chocolate shop owner.

61
00:05:08,975 --> 00:05:11,019
You haven't reached
your happily ever after yet?

62
00:05:11,102 --> 00:05:14,605
I don't need my body anymore!

63
00:05:14,689 --> 00:05:17,400
She's always been in my dreams.

64
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:20,069
Snow White, my darling!

65
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,654
- And that's how the story goes!
- And that's how the story goes!

66
00:05:21,738 --> 00:05:23,823
- And that's how the story goes!
- And that's how the story goes!

67
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:26,075
Did they just say "story?"

68
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:34,959
How could you be so cruel?

69
00:05:47,138 --> 00:05:51,768
How could you
devour my brothers like that?

70
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,479
What is this creature?

71
00:06:04,655 --> 00:06:07,408
I thought that was chocolate
I injected into my face.

72
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:09,494
Are they goats, or are they chocolate?

73
00:06:10,203 --> 00:06:13,206
"He's a cunning little devil."

74
00:06:13,289 --> 00:06:16,751
"He tricked the seven kids
into opening the door and came inside."

75
00:06:17,293 --> 00:06:23,716
"And then, he cornered the kids
one by one and gobbled them up!"

76
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:26,177
"The only one that survived

77
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:29,180
was the youngest kid,
who hid inside the grandfather clock!"

78
00:06:29,764 --> 00:06:32,642
I know this story!

79
00:06:33,309 --> 00:06:36,729
"When the mother goat came home,
she grew very upset!"

80
00:06:36,813 --> 00:06:41,275
"The mother held the scissors
in her cloven hoof,

81
00:06:41,359 --> 00:06:43,236
and went a one, a two at his stomach."

82
00:06:43,820 --> 00:06:47,198
"She took out his guts and
stuffed pebbles in his body."

83
00:06:47,281 --> 00:06:49,408
"Then he got thrown into a pond!"

84
00:06:49,492 --> 00:06:52,203
Don't read such a story!

85
00:07:06,217 --> 00:07:08,386
The villain was a wolf!

86
00:07:08,970 --> 00:07:11,931
The wolf came and ate my brothers!

87
00:07:14,475 --> 00:07:19,147
The enemy Stand wasn't going
after my body.

88
00:07:19,730 --> 00:07:21,858
I was being dragged into

89
00:07:22,733 --> 00:07:24,819
a story!

90
00:07:28,072 --> 00:07:29,449
Excuse me.

91
00:07:29,532 --> 00:07:32,160
Is this the way to
the hospital in Saint-Rémy?

92
00:07:32,243 --> 00:07:33,744
Ask someone else.

93
00:07:33,828 --> 00:07:36,164
Oh? Excuse me.

94
00:07:36,247 --> 00:07:39,542
Wait, I believe you know me.

95
00:07:39,625 --> 00:07:42,462
Sorry, but I can't help you.

96
00:07:42,545 --> 00:07:44,922
I'm not from here.

97
00:07:45,006 --> 00:07:47,341
Never mind that.

98
00:07:47,425 --> 00:07:49,469
Aren't you my fan?

99
00:07:49,552 --> 00:07:53,347
I can tell from your face.
You've been inspired by me.

100
00:07:55,516 --> 00:07:57,101
My name

101
00:07:57,185 --> 00:08:00,605
is Van Gogh.
I am Van Gogh's self-portrait.

102
00:08:00,688 --> 00:08:04,108
Yesterday, I cut off my ear with a razor.

103
00:08:07,862 --> 00:08:12,200
See, you were moved by me again.

104
00:08:12,700 --> 00:08:17,455
Mommy's coming back with scissors!

105
00:08:17,538 --> 00:08:21,250
Our mommy's going to get you!

106
00:08:24,504 --> 00:08:27,840
Bad wolf!

107
00:08:32,637 --> 00:08:35,014
Bring it, fucker!

108
00:08:38,643 --> 00:08:43,189
Mommy! We're over here!

109
00:08:43,272 --> 00:08:46,192
We're trapped in here!

110
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:49,195
What the hell?

111
00:08:49,278 --> 00:08:51,280
Save us!

112
00:08:53,449 --> 00:08:55,451
How dare you!

113
00:08:55,535 --> 00:09:00,623
How could you eat my babies?

114
00:09:02,458 --> 00:09:04,627
Continuing report
on the fantasy hero incident.

115
00:09:05,503 --> 00:09:10,341
The incident is believed to have
started in Florida, USA, a few hours ago.

116
00:09:10,424 --> 00:09:12,426
Not only are cartoon
and story characters brought to life,

117
00:09:12,510 --> 00:09:15,513
but even figures from artworks
are being sighted.

118
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:17,890
The riches of all humanity,

119
00:09:17,974 --> 00:09:20,268
the treasures for our souls

120
00:09:20,351 --> 00:09:22,478
are vanishing!

121
00:09:24,772 --> 00:09:27,567
This User doesn't care about
causing chaos around the world.

122
00:09:27,650 --> 00:09:30,403
Their only objective
is to keep the priest safe.

123
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:33,406
The Stand itself is invincible.

124
00:09:33,948 --> 00:09:35,783
The only way to win is to strike the User!

125
00:09:36,826 --> 00:09:40,454
The User is headed north. I can sense it.

126
00:09:40,997 --> 00:09:43,207
It's moving at a pretty fast pace.

127
00:09:43,291 --> 00:09:45,126
It's getting farther away from here!

128
00:09:45,626 --> 00:09:47,044
Here's a question.

129
00:09:47,128 --> 00:09:50,798
How many self-portraits did I paint,

130
00:09:50,881 --> 00:09:52,049
before my untimely death?

131
00:09:52,133 --> 00:09:54,343
Back off, or I'll kick you!

132
00:10:00,182 --> 00:10:02,226
The answer is about 40.

133
00:10:02,977 --> 00:10:05,688
Van Gogh left that many self-portraits.

134
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:07,773
It was before I cut off an ear.

135
00:10:07,857 --> 00:10:11,152
Then I ended my 37 years of life,

136
00:10:12,528 --> 00:10:15,281
killing myself with a gun!

137
00:10:17,617 --> 00:10:20,077
I see you are one of my self-portraits.

138
00:10:20,161 --> 00:10:22,872
Hello, Van Gogh with a severed ear.

139
00:10:22,955 --> 00:10:25,082
What?

140
00:10:33,299 --> 00:10:36,594
Van Gogh shot himself in the head twice.

141
00:10:36,677 --> 00:10:38,888
A single bullet wasn't enough
to end his life.

142
00:10:39,388 --> 00:10:44,560
That's right. He needed to shoot himself
twice to seal the deal.

143
00:10:45,144 --> 00:10:47,438
This enemy!

144
00:10:48,022 --> 00:10:50,066
Weather Forecast!

145
00:10:51,025 --> 00:10:52,610
Direction is north.

146
00:10:52,693 --> 00:10:57,239
Shut down the highway with a rainstorm,
up to 30 kilometers north!

147
00:10:57,323 --> 00:11:01,369
Don't let a single car head north!

148
00:11:05,164 --> 00:11:07,667
Diver Drive restructured the door
from the inside.

149
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:11,545
It's been fused with the wall.
Nothing can open this door now!

150
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:21,180
Diver Drive!

151
00:11:27,061 --> 00:11:29,480
My brothers are free!

152
00:11:29,563 --> 00:11:31,774
And that's how the story goes!

153
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:35,736
Once a story begins,
nothing can alter its course.

154
00:11:35,820 --> 00:11:38,906
I'm powerless against this Stand!

155
00:11:40,199 --> 00:11:41,700
The walls, Diver Drive!

156
00:11:41,784 --> 00:11:43,160
Submerge!

157
00:11:48,582 --> 00:11:50,251
Hell yes, I'm safe.

158
00:11:55,923 --> 00:11:57,675
Officers from earlier.

159
00:11:58,259 --> 00:12:00,219
So their souls have also split
from their bodies.

160
00:12:00,719 --> 00:12:03,431
Anyhow, I'm taking this police car…

161
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:07,393
- Pebbles! Get the pebbles!
- Mommy!

162
00:12:07,476 --> 00:12:12,898
I can't escape.
Weather, hurry and kill the User!

163
00:12:14,233 --> 00:12:18,154
I sensed the enemy up north,

164
00:12:18,237 --> 00:12:20,448
but now it's down south.

165
00:12:20,948 --> 00:12:22,283
No way…

166
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:24,201
Is it in the air?

167
00:12:25,828 --> 00:12:28,956
Flight 8250, destination Key West.

168
00:12:29,457 --> 00:12:31,041
Despite the sudden downpour,

169
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:33,919
we were able to depart on time.

170
00:12:34,003 --> 00:12:37,214
This ability that recently awakened
within me.

171
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:41,177
I can only be defeated if
I'm in direct harm's way

172
00:12:41,260 --> 00:12:45,931
Nothing can touch me when
I'm high up in the air.

173
00:12:46,515 --> 00:12:48,392
I'm finally living my life to the fullest.

174
00:12:48,476 --> 00:12:51,479
This power keeps my blood racing.

175
00:13:01,363 --> 00:13:02,198
THE NIGHT BEFORE

176
00:13:02,281 --> 00:13:03,949
To be born

177
00:13:04,617 --> 00:13:06,535
means to be chosen.

178
00:13:07,036 --> 00:13:09,622
Once one is chosen,

179
00:13:09,705 --> 00:13:11,749
one is protected and supported by all.

180
00:13:12,333 --> 00:13:14,752
Amidst the competitions of life,

181
00:13:15,336 --> 00:13:16,587
the chosen one rises above.

182
00:13:17,880 --> 00:13:20,799
Those who were drawn to me.

183
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:25,721
They exist to bring me to heaven
when the rightful time arrives.

184
00:13:26,514 --> 00:13:30,851
Yes, Jolyne Cujoh may have escaped
to chase me down,

185
00:13:30,935 --> 00:13:33,687
but she merely exists
to help me attain heaven.

186
00:13:34,438 --> 00:13:36,023
Sons of Dio,

187
00:13:36,607 --> 00:13:40,361
help me get to Cape Canaveral.

188
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:45,324
This act will be
your singular source of joy.

189
00:13:45,908 --> 00:13:47,034
All my life,

190
00:13:47,117 --> 00:13:52,248
I felt like a tumbling rock
that rolls without a purpose.

191
00:13:54,083 --> 00:13:56,877
But now I understand.

192
00:13:56,961 --> 00:14:00,130
I was born to use my ability!

193
00:14:00,214 --> 00:14:02,508
I'll do whatever it takes
to protect the priest.

194
00:14:02,591 --> 00:14:06,470
Also, Bohemian Ecstatic is magnificent!

195
00:14:06,554 --> 00:14:09,682
It makes me laugh to watch
society fall into utter darkness.

196
00:14:09,765 --> 00:14:14,812
The very society that despised me!

197
00:14:15,604 --> 00:14:18,023
No, I can't catch up.

198
00:14:18,732 --> 00:14:21,193
If the Stand User is on an airplane,

199
00:14:21,277 --> 00:14:22,987
its speed exceeds 400kph.

200
00:14:23,696 --> 00:14:26,365
Even the largest hurricane on record

201
00:14:26,448 --> 00:14:28,075
cannot travel faster than 280kph.

202
00:14:28,659 --> 00:14:31,328
There's not a single weather phenomenon
that can catch up to an airplane.

203
00:14:31,912 --> 00:14:33,080
It got away!

204
00:14:34,790 --> 00:14:35,791
One more bullet.

205
00:14:36,625 --> 00:14:38,419
If I take one more bullet,

206
00:14:38,502 --> 00:14:40,045
this story will end.

207
00:14:40,129 --> 00:14:41,338
Dammit!

208
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:44,633
Don't you dare get close to that gun.

209
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:46,510
If you touch it, I'll kill you!

210
00:15:00,566 --> 00:15:01,442
Anastasia!

211
00:15:02,443 --> 00:15:03,903
Weather.

212
00:15:08,782 --> 00:15:10,951
What?

213
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:25,007
Weather!

214
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:33,015
Yes! The wolf is drowned!

215
00:15:33,098 --> 00:15:35,517
- And that's how the story goes!
- Hurray!

216
00:15:36,101 --> 00:15:39,063
It's over. That's how the end goes.

217
00:15:39,647 --> 00:15:42,858
I'll live a happy life in your place.

218
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,527
According to the experts,

219
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:48,280
the city with the most damage
due to the fantasy hero incident…

220
00:15:48,781 --> 00:15:52,201
What is your wish, Aladdin?

221
00:15:52,284 --> 00:15:55,955
I am your loyal servant.

222
00:15:56,038 --> 00:16:00,042
- I can grant any wish.
- Shut up, brat!

223
00:16:01,835 --> 00:16:04,505
What are you reading? Let me see.

224
00:16:07,049 --> 00:16:09,051
I can't breathe!

225
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:10,719
You want me to do more?

226
00:16:11,303 --> 00:16:15,015
No, this is fine. Thanks.

227
00:16:15,099 --> 00:16:17,351
You've got real talent.

228
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:21,146
What's with the drawing, Weather?

229
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:23,482
I got this Van Gogh to draw,

230
00:16:23,565 --> 00:16:26,110
and create a new character.

231
00:16:26,735 --> 00:16:28,654
He comes with a story of his own.

232
00:16:28,737 --> 00:16:31,448
This hero can use an ability.

233
00:16:31,532 --> 00:16:35,995
It sucks all the fantasy heroes
back into their stories!

234
00:16:46,005 --> 00:16:48,215
This hero's story will end

235
00:16:48,799 --> 00:16:51,135
once its ability restores order
to our reality!

236
00:16:54,722 --> 00:16:57,766
We're going back,
and that's how the story goes.

237
00:16:57,850 --> 00:17:02,229
We will now rejoin our unharmed bodies!

238
00:17:10,070 --> 00:17:11,947
Hey, are you listening?

239
00:17:12,531 --> 00:17:14,908
Can I have my book back?

240
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:17,369
Breaking news.

241
00:17:17,453 --> 00:17:19,872
Order has been restored.

242
00:17:19,955 --> 00:17:22,374
Characters from story books,
cartoons, movies, and artwork

243
00:17:22,458 --> 00:17:23,917
are back where they belong.

244
00:17:24,001 --> 00:17:28,547
This includes Mona Lisa, Snow White,
Batman, and Tweety.

245
00:17:29,548 --> 00:17:33,802
However, for some unknown reason,
Pinocchio is still missing.

246
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:35,554
Did you fall asleep?

247
00:17:35,637 --> 00:17:37,056
Was it too boring?

248
00:17:37,639 --> 00:17:40,851
But this story is full
of hopes and dreams.

249
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:42,311
UNGALO
STAND NAME: BOHEMIAN ECSTATIC

250
00:17:42,394 --> 00:17:44,021
BACK TO DESPAIR
BEYOND RECOVERY

251
00:17:50,861 --> 00:17:54,990
Hey, what do you drive now?

252
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:58,702
I hope

253
00:17:58,786 --> 00:18:02,664
you got rid of that one, Romeo.

254
00:18:03,248 --> 00:18:05,417
Jolyne!

255
00:18:05,501 --> 00:18:07,795
Please. Help me, Jolyne!

256
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:12,674
- Do you know what a "plea deal" is?
- …you will be sent to Green Dolphin…

257
00:18:12,758 --> 00:18:14,676
Romeo!

258
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,178
You…

259
00:18:16,762 --> 00:18:17,721
How did you…

260
00:18:18,263 --> 00:18:19,765
Let me warn you, Romeo.

261
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:21,934
Stay away from the phone.

262
00:18:22,601 --> 00:18:23,894
All phones.

263
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:25,312
Got that?

264
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:28,107
That's the last thing on my mind.

265
00:18:28,190 --> 00:18:31,110
Ever since that day, I've felt so sorry.

266
00:18:31,693 --> 00:18:33,904
I realized my own foolishness

267
00:18:33,987 --> 00:18:38,408
only after I lost you.

268
00:18:39,576 --> 00:18:41,620
Oh, god.

269
00:18:41,703 --> 00:18:45,541
How can I ever make up
for what I've done to you--

270
00:18:47,251 --> 00:18:49,586
There's no need for words, Romeo.

271
00:18:52,256 --> 00:18:55,300
You are the best I ever had.

272
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:57,803
I need you.

273
00:18:58,762 --> 00:19:01,932
I tried to go visit you,
but they wouldn't let me.

274
00:19:02,015 --> 00:19:05,394
Romeo, you poor boy.

275
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:08,355
I really pity you.

276
00:19:09,481 --> 00:19:11,733
Nothing matters anymore

277
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:13,694
about the hit-and-run.

278
00:19:14,194 --> 00:19:17,114
I have nothing against you.

279
00:19:17,614 --> 00:19:20,367
After all, you got embroiled
in a conspiracy.

280
00:19:20,993 --> 00:19:25,414
Romeo, I came to ask you for a favor.

281
00:19:25,497 --> 00:19:27,332
I need money and a car.

282
00:19:28,417 --> 00:19:30,460
I have to go somewhere.

283
00:19:34,089 --> 00:19:36,508
I only have a thousand dollars on me.

284
00:19:37,676 --> 00:19:39,011
Take these keys.

285
00:19:39,094 --> 00:19:41,430
This is plenty. Thank you, Romeo.

286
00:19:42,222 --> 00:19:44,099
Just don't talk if the police come.

287
00:19:44,766 --> 00:19:45,767
Promise me.

288
00:19:46,351 --> 00:19:47,811
Oh, Jolyne,

289
00:19:47,895 --> 00:19:49,813
I will confess my crimes.

290
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:51,899
I'll get you a non-guilty verdict.

291
00:19:51,982 --> 00:19:54,109
So please, come back to me!

292
00:20:08,582 --> 00:20:10,459
Wow, car keys!

293
00:20:11,418 --> 00:20:15,797
Hello? I'm Romeo Jisso,
a Palm Beach resident.

294
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:17,674
Is this the police?

295
00:20:18,467 --> 00:20:20,677
I'm reporting an escaped convict.

296
00:20:20,761 --> 00:20:23,263
Yes, it's Jolyne Cujoh.

297
00:20:24,389 --> 00:20:25,599
I knew it.

298
00:20:25,682 --> 00:20:29,686
It was wise that you used my sticker
to make a copy of his tongue.

299
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:32,606
This asshole is already ratting you out.

300
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:34,775
No, she didn't!

301
00:20:34,858 --> 00:20:37,694
She didn't come to my house.
Why would she?

302
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:41,907
I'm filing a report because she called.

303
00:20:41,990 --> 00:20:43,492
Yes, we only talked over the phone.

304
00:20:43,575 --> 00:20:46,245
She asked for money
but I didn't give her any.

305
00:20:46,745 --> 00:20:48,872
She said she's headed to Mexico.

306
00:20:49,665 --> 00:20:52,668
Of course, I will make another call
if she contacts me again.

307
00:20:54,169 --> 00:20:56,129
Yes. Bye.

308
00:20:56,213 --> 00:20:58,215
I'm impressed.

309
00:20:58,298 --> 00:21:00,133
He kept his word.

310
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:02,886
I will do anything for her.

311
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:04,346
Anything to atone for my actions.

312
00:21:06,515 --> 00:21:08,058
Jolyne!

313
00:21:08,642 --> 00:21:11,353
Wow, your ex-boyfriend is awesome!

314
00:21:11,436 --> 00:21:12,854
Guess what the key is for?

315
00:21:12,938 --> 00:21:15,565
He gave us car keys too, but guess what?

316
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:17,359
Look over there!

317
00:21:21,321 --> 00:21:23,615
Can we ride it?

318
00:21:23,699 --> 00:21:25,325
I want to try piloting it.

319
00:21:25,409 --> 00:21:29,705
I bet it's totally different
from reading about it in a book!

320
00:21:31,873 --> 00:21:35,794
Romeo, I stand corrected.

321
00:21:38,797 --> 00:21:41,717
But let's rip this off. For good measure.

322
00:21:47,597 --> 00:21:48,724
Let's get going.

323
00:21:49,558 --> 00:21:52,102
The helicopter will get us there
in a matter of hours.

324
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:27,447
Father,

325
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:30,325
I understand my assignment to protect you.

326
00:23:31,034 --> 00:23:33,745
Can you do something
about my eyelid first?

327
00:23:34,329 --> 00:23:35,664
One of my eyelids

328
00:23:36,373 --> 00:23:37,791
always slides down for no reason.

329
00:23:38,416 --> 00:23:40,085
I can't open my eye.

330
00:23:41,336 --> 00:23:43,255
I mean, I can get it to open sometimes.

331
00:23:43,338 --> 00:23:47,968
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
